{"id":427,"date":"2022-04-22T12:16:59","date_gmt":"2022-04-22T12:16:59","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/?page_id=427"},"modified":"2026-07-14T06:08:04","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T06:08:04","slug":"counselling-services","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/counselling-services\/","title":{"rendered":"Counselling Services"},"content":{"rendered":"\r\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"text-align: left;\">The <strong>Student Counselling Cell<\/strong> at the <strong>Federal Institute of Science and Technology (FISAT)<\/strong> is dedicated to promoting the mental health, emotional well-being, and overall development of students. We provide a safe, confidential, and non-judgmental space where students can discuss academic, personal, emotional, or psychological concerns and receive professional support.<\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Counselling is a collaborative process that helps students understand themselves better, manage stress, build resilience, develop healthy coping strategies, and make informed decisions. Guided by the principles of empathy, respect, confidentiality, and professional ethics, the Counselling Cell encourages students to seek help whenever they need support.<\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Cell is led by a <strong>full-time qualified Mental Health Counsellor (Psychologist)<\/strong> and works in collaboration with faculty mentors, Heads of Departments, hostel authorities, parents, and healthcare professionals, whenever required, to foster a healthy, supportive, and student-friendly campus environment.<\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong><u>Services &amp; Activities<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">\u00a0<strong>Individual Counselling:<\/strong> Confidential one-to-one counselling for students facing academic, emotional, personal, behavioural, relationship, career, or mental health concerns.<\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Group Counselling &amp; Workshops:<\/strong> Interactive sessions, orientation programmes, and awareness workshops on stress management, emotional well-being, life skills, communication, and personal development.<\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Crisis Support:<\/strong> Providing immediate psychological support during emotional crises and facilitating appropriate intervention when necessary.<\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Student Counselling Committee<\/strong><\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Student Counseling Committee consists of faculty representatives from each department who work with the Mental Health Counselor to support student well-being, facilitate referrals, and promote mental health awareness across the campus.<\/p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/Remitha.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-8150\" src=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/Remitha.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"198\" height=\"255\" srcset=\"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/Remitha.jpg 413w, https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/Remitha-233x300.jpg 233w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 198px) 100vw, 198px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Ms. Remitha Rajan P T<br \/>Counsellor<br \/><\/strong><\/p>\r\n<p>Ms. Remitha Rajan P T is a psychologist with 10 years of clinical experience in field of Mental health. She was worked with ASTER MIMS hospital kottakal as psychologist for 6 years and also with <strong>INDIAN INSTITUTE OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, <\/strong>Kottayam(IIITK) as student psychologist for two years, presently working with FISAT engineering college as a Student Counsellor.<br \/>She completed her MSc in Psychology &amp; MSW specialization in Medical &amp; Psychiatry from Calicut University. Her areas of interest are adult and adolescent mental health &#8211; anxiety and stress related disorders, obsessive compulsive disorder and depression, Personality disorders, marital and family counselling, adolescent adjustment issues, Assessment of Learning difficulty and remedial training, suicidal preventions.<\/p>\r\n<p>In 2013, she was selected as the student counselor for the <strong>&#8216;Kerala School Kalolsavam&#8217;<\/strong> held in Malappuram, representing Aster MIMS. She has conducted numerous workshops and training programs for healthcare workers, clinical trainees and for students.<\/p>\r\n\r\n\r\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Student Counselling Cell at the Federal Institute of Science and Technology (FISAT) is dedicated to promoting the mental health, emotional well-being, and overall development of students. We provide a safe, confidential, and non-judgmental space where students can discuss academic, personal, emotional, or psychological concerns and receive professional support. Counselling is a collaborative process that [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"campus.php","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-427","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/427","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/2"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=427"}],"version-history":[{"count":12,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/427\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12329,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/427\/revisions\/12329"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/m